DESCRIPTION:Prize winning author Gus Speth will present and read from his 
 new novel\, Jericho River\, a story about a Vermont village in the 1960s a
 nd 70's that the Washington Posts calls "a great read." On Amazon\, author
  Jonathan Lash says of Jericho River: "With a poet’s pen and humane sens
 ibility Gus Speth creates Our Town for the 21st Century. Jericho River is 
 a gentle narrative despite the intrusion of a threatening world\, a tale t
 hat leaves its readers with hope."\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:The Norwich Bookstore\, 291 Main St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/new-vermon
 t-novel-to-be-presented-at-norwich-bookstore-22-10-2026-12-50-15
