BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Architecture + Design Film Series: The Desert of Forbidden Art
DTSTART:20261111T183000
DTEND:20261111T203000
DTSTAMP:20261110T184334Z
UID:dc9cc442e0844e388615d6d911feeb@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:During Stalin’s Soviet era\, Igor Savitsky collected more th
 an 40\,000 beautiful\, colorful\, powerful and rarely seen works by artist
 s experimenting in a brash\, avant-garde style. These works\, at odds with
  the drab realism favored by the government\, put the artists at great ris
 k. Savitsky searched out the artists and their works and created a museum 
 in Uzbekistan\, remote enough that he evaded the worst of Soviet censorshi
 p. He collected and preserved cultural artifacts of Uzbeks as the governme
 nt attempted to erase the culture. This film follows his story\, taking us
  on a dramatic journey of sacrifice for the sake of creative freedom\, whi
 le revealing the glorious works of art and the stories of the people invol
 ved. Screen from Home\, Same Day Only Directed by Tchavdar Georgiev & Aman
 da Pope 2011\, Russia\, USA\, Uzbekistan\, 80 Minutes Learn more about the
  Season 14 of The Architecture + Design Film Series at adfilmseries.org\n
 \nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Contois Auditorium\, City Hall\, 149 Church St Hall\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/architectu
 re-design-film-series-the-desert-of-forbidden-art-07-10-2026-15-04-29
END:VEVENT
